/**
 * @file triad_count_make_test_test.cpp
 * @brief ESCHER-GPU's `make test` replayed in hosted CI on the host backends (M9a step 4; PLAN
 *        8.3; decision D5): the make-test groups regenerated by generators::legacy (the input and
 *        A's batches, drawn from a host model in step with the hypergraph), checked exactly
 *        against A's committed counts (cpp/tests/data/goldens/triad_counts/
 *        escher_gpu_make_test.txt, written by parity/triad_goldens.py fixture) and against the
 *        independent oracle, with "baseline + deltas == compute()" and check_integrity() after
 *        every batch.
 *
 * Groups 01, 03, 07 and 12 have synthetic inputs (A's positional arguments n m r1 r2): their
 * counts must equal A's. The file-input groups (04-11, 13-15) read inputs A's test script writes
 * with awk's random numbers, which the library does not reproduce; their shapes are regenerated
 * here (the small file as generators::legacy's hypergraph of the same parameters and awk's seed,
 * the skewed and medium files by their recipes with a std::mt19937_64) and replayed with A's batch
 * options against the oracle.
 *
 * Two executables (cpp/tests/algorithms/triad_count/CMakeLists.txt): dyng_triad_count_make_test_
 * tests (label cpu, hosted CI) runs every pattern on the small groups and the patterns without
 * triangles (types 1 and 2) on the syn100k, skewed and medium groups; built with
 * DYNG_TRIAD_MAKE_TEST_LARGE it is dyng_triad_count_make_test_large_tests (labels parity, slow),
 * which runs the triangle patterns (h_motif, type 3) on those groups: a full count of the skewed
 * group's 1,200-hyperedge clique of the line graph alone takes seconds.
 */
